Run this example in a fresh database:
```sql
PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;
CREATE TABLE people(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL);
CREATE TABLE clubs(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL);
INSERT INTO people VALUES (1, 'Mira'), (2, 'Oren');
INSERT INTO clubs VALUES (10, 'Art'), (20, 'Music');
CREATE TABLE membership (
  person_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES people(id),
  club_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES clubs(id),
  PRIMARY KEY(person_id, club_id)
);
INSERT INTO membership VALUES (1, 10), (1, 20), (2, 10);
SELECT p.name, c.title
FROM membership AS m
JOIN people AS p ON p.id = m.person_id
JOIN clubs AS c ON c.id = m.club_id
ORDER BY p.name, c.title;
```
The result is Mira/Art, Mira/Music, and Oren/Art. The joins turn the stored IDs into names.
